at 7,812, up 0.6%.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:40.440
The NASDAQ composite closed at 27,366, up 0.6%.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:47.200
The TSX composite closed at 35,665, up 1.5%.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:52.320
Sentiment today reflects mixed earnings momentum and ongoing central bank policy paths

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:55.280
from both the Bank of Canada and the Federal Reserve.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:00.660
Rate-sensitive sectors continue to face pressure while select consumer names show resilience

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.900
on guidance upgrades.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:07.940
The central bank backdrop remains the key frame for rate-sensitive holdings in TFSA accounts.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:13.760
Valuation screening identifies stocks trading below estimated fair value using discounted

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.040
cash flow models and peer multiples.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:21.020
Today's market conditions make this relevant because several Canadian retailers reported

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:26.300
earnings beats that widen the gap between current prices and analysts derived fair values.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.980
To implement it, open a screener on your brokerage platform, filter for companies with positive

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:37.480
earning surprises and cash-rich balance sheets, then compare the last close to the reported fair

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:43.340
value estimate. This approach worked well during the 2022 rate hike cycle when depressed multiples

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:49.240
provided a buffer against further declines. Risks include model assumptions that prove too optimistic

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:55.520
if revenue growth slows. For a TFSA holder, apply the screen to names already on your watchlist,

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:59.160
and size positions at $1,000 to maintain discipline.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:04.020
Eritzia reported a 20.5% single-day jump after the results,

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:08.540
moving the share price to $146.91 Canadian dollars.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:13.680
The fair value estimate stands at $185.21 Canadian dollars,

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.540
leaving a sizeable discount even after the move.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:23.960
Imagine you bought a high-growth tech name last week after an AI-related announcement and watched it gap higher on volume.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:31.960
The mechanism that actually determines whether that move sustains is the difference between revenue-backed cash flow and pure narrative multiples.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:38.880
Exactly as it was in 1999 when many internet stocks traded at hundreds of times sales with no profits.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:44.020
benefits. A pro insight is to check the ratio of enterprise value to next 12 months revenue

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:49.200
against the sector median before adding to a position. If the multiple sits more than

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:55.580
50% above peers with similar growth, the setup carries extra downside. The concrete misconception

00:02:55.580 --> 00:03:01.540
to avoid is assuming every AI company will compound like the survivors. The fix is to demand

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:06.580
visible revenue and free cash flow traction before treating the name as a long-term holding.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:12.100
surviving. Survivors such as Amazon maintained real revenue streams, while many others collapsed

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:17.220
when funding dried up. Today's AI names differ because most already generate measurable

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:22.720
sales, yet the valuation discipline lesson remains identical. Investors who applied the

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:29.340
same check in 2022 avoided the sharpest drawdowns in unprofitable growth names. This is a simulated

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:34.800
trade for educational purposes only. No real money is involved. We are looking at Eritzia

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:38.320
on the TSX under the ticker ATZ.TO.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:42.000
The sector is consumer, the strategy family is valuation.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:48.340
The catalyst is the Q2 sales beat, net income jump from tariff refunds, and raised fiscal

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:49.640
